{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 4958062,
  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34676054",
      "title": "Protecting Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 99,
      "videoOrder": 92,
      "sourceHash": "88a8487f35100e3f8ae77503313e8d040342bb2eb986f42094532bf0c4523f8e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.11,
          "en": "So we're making good progress here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.11,
          "end": 6.72,
          "en": "We're using this session information to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.72,
          "end": 8.373,
          "en": "for example, update the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.33,
          "end": 12.15,
          "en": "Now one thing that's of course still possible here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.15,
          "end": 15.96,
          "en": "is that we visit our expenses page without being logged in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.96,
          "end": 17.67,
          "en": "I mean it shows the logout button here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.67,
          "end": 20.64,
          "en": "but here the button is hard coded in this navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.64,
          "end": 22.983,
          "en": "that's shown for the expenses pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.94,
          "end": 25.38,
          "en": "If you go back to the starting page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.38,
          "end": 28.47,
          "en": "we see that we actually are not logged in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.47,
          "end": 31.11,
          "en": "but still we can go to the expenses page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.11,
          "end": 33.497,
          "en": "Now, it would make sense to protect this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.497,
          "end": 36.51,
          "en": "and also the analysis page here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.51,
          "end": 40.47,
          "en": "or the ad expense page against unauthenticated access,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.47,
          "end": 42.9,
          "en": "so that users who are not logged in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.9,
          "end": 45.21,
          "en": "are not able to visit these pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.21,
          "end": 46.8,
          "en": "Because they also should not be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.8,
          "end": 51.363,
          "en": "to create new expenses or load expenses, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.44,
          "end": 56.25,
          "en": "So, to make sure that certain pages are not accessible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.25,
          "end": 61.25,
          "en": "we can use their loaders to block navigation to these pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.473,
          "end": 65.16,
          "en": "For example, the expenses jsx route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.16,
          "end": 68.88,
          "en": "There we have a loader where we get our expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.88,
          "end": 71.67,
          "en": "And here it would make sense to first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.67,
          "end": 74.22,
          "en": "check whether we have a logged in user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.22,
          "end": 75.78,
          "en": "And if that's not the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.78,
          "end": 77.82,
          "en": "I want to not continue at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.82,
          "end": 80.16,
          "en": "Instead, I want to redirect the user away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.16,
          "end": 82.59,
          "en": "and not grant access to this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.59,
          "end": 86.22,
          "en": "it's sub pages, or my expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.22,
          "end": 89.82,
          "en": "To achieve this, I'll get back to auth server js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.82,
          "end": 92.81,
          "en": "And in there I'll add yet another new function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.81,
          "end": 95.88,
          "en": "which is exported in async,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.88,
          "end": 100.22999999999999,
          "en": "which could be called require user session",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.22999999999999,
          "end": 103.32300000000001,
          "en": "and which gets a request object as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.85,
          "end": 105.93,
          "en": "With that argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.93,
          "end": 110.61,
          "en": "I'll call get user from session and pass my request to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.61,
          "end": 113.67,
          "en": "So that is one of these functions we created earlier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.67,
          "end": 114.753,
          "en": "this function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.97999999999999,
          "end": 117.99000000000001,
          "en": "So, I create my user from that session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.99000000000001,
          "end": 120.42,
          "en": "And this function, as you might recall,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.42,
          "end": 122.673,
          "en": "returns null if we have no user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.66,
          "end": 126.12,
          "en": "So therefore here, in require user session,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.12,
          "end": 128.73,
          "en": "I'll wait calling this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.73,
          "end": 130.24099999999999,
          "en": "and then here, I get my user ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.24099999999999,
          "end": 133.383,
          "en": "This could be null though, if we have no user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.25,
          "end": 137.913,
          "en": "So therefore, I'll then check if user ID is not set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.93,
          "end": 140.22,
          "en": "So if it's null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.22,
          "end": 143.493,
          "en": "in which case I know that the user is not logged in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.45,
          "end": 147.21,
          "en": "Now, since I named this require user session,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.21,
          "end": 151.38,
          "en": "I want to be able to call this function as a guard basically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.38,
          "end": 155.46,
          "en": "so that this require user session function froze an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.46,
          "end": 160.46,
          "en": "or redirects the user away if the user is not authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.65,
          "end": 164.103,
          "en": "And this can be achieved by throwing a redirect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.63,
          "end": 167.85,
          "en": "Now this is something we haven't done before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.85,
          "end": 170.49,
          "en": "Thus far, we threw normal responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.49,
          "end": 172.211,
          "en": "and we return to redirects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.211,
          "end": 175.68,
          "en": "but we can also throw redirects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.68,
          "end": 180.68,
          "en": "If we do that, we won't trigger a catch boundary, actually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.69,
          "end": 183.9,
          "en": "but instead the user will simply be redirected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.9,
          "end": 185.91,
          "en": "as he or she always would.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.91,
          "end": 188.609,
          "en": "But we cancel this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.609,
          "end": 191.16,
          "en": "because that's the default behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.16,
          "end": 193.68,
          "en": "If we throw, we cancel this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 193.68,
          "end": 196.26,
          "en": "and any functions where this is getting called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.26,
          "end": 198.75,
          "en": "and Remix will see that we a redirect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.75,
          "end": 203.01,
          "en": "and just perform that redirect, but halt all our operations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 203.01,
          "end": 205.86,
          "en": "So with that, we ensure that we don't continue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.86,
          "end": 208.953,
          "en": "loading expense data or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.88,
          "end": 212.34,
          "en": "So here, I throw a redirect to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 212.34,
          "end": 216.153,
          "en": "slash auth and there may be mode set equal to login.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.65,
          "end": 220.02,
          "en": "With this simple function added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 220.02,
          "end": 223.2,
          "en": "we can go back to expenses jsx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 223.2,
          "end": 225.42000000000002,
          "en": "and there in the loader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 225.42000000000002,
          "end": 228.78300000000002,
          "en": "we can now call require user session,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.74,
          "end": 232.35,
          "en": "get our request here out of the object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.35,
          "end": 233.73,
          "en": "passed to the loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 233.73,
          "end": 237.75,
          "en": "and pass this request to require user session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 237.75,
          "end": 240.81,
          "en": "And since this will throw a redirect if it fails,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 240.81,
          "end": 244.38,
          "en": "there's nothing else we have to do besides awaiting it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 244.38,
          "end": 245.523,
          "en": "That's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 246.78,
          "end": 249.99,
          "en": "So, we will make it pass this function call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 249.99,
          "end": 252.87,
          "en": "if we have a valid user, and in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 252.87,
          "end": 255.54,
          "en": "we'll continue fetching our expenses and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 255.54,
          "end": 258.425,
          "en": "But otherwise, this redirect response will be thrown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 258.425,
          "end": 260.91,
          "en": "and will be performed by Remix",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 260.91,
          "end": 264.033,
          "en": "and will not grant access to the expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 265.5,
          "end": 269.76,
          "en": "So here, if I try to visit my expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 269.76,
          "end": 271.62,
          "en": "by clicking this link, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 271.62,
          "end": 273.63,
          "en": "I instead end up on the off page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 273.63,
          "end": 275.1,
          "en": "And the same thing happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 275.1,
          "end": 277.443,
          "en": "if I manually enter slash expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 278.58,
          "end": 282.03,
          "en": "If I enter slash expenses slash add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 282.03,
          "end": 283.59000000000003,
          "en": "the same thing happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 283.59000000000003,
          "end": 286.56,
          "en": "because that is a child route of my expenses route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 286.56,
          "end": 290.073,
          "en": "So these routes are automatically also protected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 291.24,
          "end": 293.46,
          "en": "However, there is one very important note",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 293.46,
          "end": 297.39,
          "en": "about the loaders of these child routes, if they had any.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 297.39,
          "end": 298.74,
          "en": "If they had loaders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.74,
          "end": 301.377,
          "en": "these loaders would still start to execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 301.377,
          "end": 304.05,
          "en": "before we're redirected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 304.05,
          "end": 307.59,
          "en": "Because if you have nested routes with nested loaders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 307.59,
          "end": 310.83,
          "en": "so loaders in the parent and the child routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 310.83,
          "end": 315.15,
          "en": "those loaders are called in parallel by Remix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 315.15,
          "end": 316.59,
          "en": "And I can show this to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 316.59,
          "end": 319.89,
          "en": "If I add a loader to my add route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 319.89,
          "end": 322.8,
          "en": "if I export a function loader here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 322.8,
          "end": 326.37,
          "en": "and I simply console lock add loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 326.37,
          "end": 329.13,
          "en": "and then I return null here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 329.13,
          "end": 332.133,
          "en": "you will see that if we take a look at the terminal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 333.03,
          "end": 338.03,
          "en": "if I visit slash expenses slash ad, the redirect works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 339.84000000000003,
          "end": 343.02,
          "en": "But you actually see ad loader here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 343.02,
          "end": 344.76800000000003,
          "en": "in the terminal nonetheless.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 344.76800000000003,
          "end": 348.21,
          "en": "So this loader started to execute and depending",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 348.21,
          "end": 352.02,
          "en": "on what it does, it probably also finished executing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 352.02,
          "end": 353.771,
          "en": "And that's important to keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 353.771,
          "end": 356.01,
          "en": "Even though their redirect worked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 356.01,
          "end": 360.06,
          "en": "your nested loaders could still start executing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 360.06,
          "end": 362.61,
          "en": "And depending on what they do, that could be a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 362.61,
          "end": 366.54,
          "en": "If you are fetching data in there that should be protected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 366.54,
          "end": 368.79,
          "en": "well then, you started fetching that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 368.79,
          "end": 370.933,
          "en": "even though the user might not be logged in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 370.933,
          "end": 373.62,
          "en": "That can lead to errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 373.62,
          "end": 375,
          "en": "Or in the worst case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 375,
          "end": 377.79,
          "en": "you might even return that data to the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 377.79,
          "end": 380.19,
          "en": "And indeed then it would be accessible there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 380.19,
          "end": 382.503,
          "en": "even though a redirect occurs thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 383.46,
          "end": 386.79,
          "en": "So therefore, if you have nested routes with nested loaders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 386.79,
          "end": 391.79,
          "en": "you must add this user session check to all your loaders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 391.8,
          "end": 394.44,
          "en": "not just to the loader in the parent route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 394.44,
          "end": 398.49,
          "en": "That's not enough because since loaders run in parallel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 398.49,
          "end": 402.06,
          "en": "in order to speed things up, nested loaders will run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 402.06,
          "end": 405.12,
          "en": "even if the parent loader eventually fails",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 405.12,
          "end": 406.383,
          "en": "and throws an error.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
